// This example builds a https://vaadin.com/flow[Vaadin Flow] web application
// running on Spring Boot, using the `mill-contrib-vaadin` plugin. Mixing in
// `mill.contrib.vaadin.VaadinModule` adds:
//
// * `vaadinBuildFrontend`: Vaadin's production frontend build, the equivalent of
//   the `prepare-frontend` and `build-frontend` goals of the Maven plugin. It runs
//   `npm install` and bundles the frontend with Vite into `META-INF/VAADIN`
// * `vaadinPackage`: a self-contained production distribution with the
//   application jar, its dependencies, the frontend bundle and a launch script
// * Vaadin development mode for `./mill run`
//
// Development-only dependencies such as `com.vaadin:vaadin-dev` go into
// `runMvnDeps`: `./mill run` uses them, while the production frontend build and
// `vaadinPackage` leave them out.

/** See Also: build.mill.yaml */

/** See Also: src/com/example/Application.java */

/** See Also: src/com/example/MainView.java */

// The frontend build uses the Flow version of the application's classpath, here
// managed by `vaadin-bom`. Vaadin's build tooling requires Java 21, hence the
// `mill-jvm-version` above.
//
// Frontend sources such as themes, stylesheets or TypeScript views go into
// `frontend/`, next to `src/` and `resources/`; Vaadin also generates files into
// `frontend/generated/`. A `MavenModule` uses Vaadin's default `src/main/frontend`
// instead, and `vaadinFrontendDir` can point anywhere else.

/** Usage

> ./mill show vaadinFlowVersion
"25.3.0"

> ./mill runBackground

> for i in $(seq 1 300); do curl -sf localhost:${PORT:-8080} -o page.html && ! grep -q devServerIsNotLoaded page.html && break; sleep 1; done # mac/linux

> curl http://localhost:${PORT:-8080} # mac/linux
...window.Vaadin.developmentMode = true;...

> ls frontend/generated # mac/linux
...jar-resources...

> ./mill clean runBackground

> ./mill vaadinBuildFrontend
...

> ls out/vaadinFrontendBuild.dest/servlet-resources/META-INF/VAADIN/config
...flow-build-info.json...

> ./mill show vaadinPackage
...out/vaadinPackage.dest/dist...

> ls out/vaadinPackage.dest/dist
app.jar
lib
run-prod.sh
vaadin-frontend

> ./out/vaadinPackage.dest/dist/run-prod.sh > prod.log 2>&1 & echo $! > prod.pid # mac/linux

> curl http://localhost:${PORT:-8080} # mac/linux
...<script type="module" crossorigin src="VAADIN/build/indexhtml-...

> kill $(cat prod.pid) # mac/linux

*/

// The distribution runs the application in Vaadin's production mode:
//
// [source,console]
// ----
// > ./out/vaadinPackage.dest/dist/run-prod.sh
// ----
